AB Download Manager
-------------------
This product includes code and behavior derived from AB Download Manager,
Copyright the AB Download Manager contributors, licensed under the Apache
License, Version 2.0.

  https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager
  https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager-browser-integration
  https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0

No AB Download Manager source file is copied verbatim. The browser-capture
extension in this repository re-implements AB's download-interception pipeline
in JavaScript with SAYL's own native-messaging/host bridge protocol retained.
Every file listed below carries the header comment:

  Portions derived from AB Download Manager
  (https://github.com/amir1376/ab-download-manager), Apache-2.0

What was derived, and from where:

  extensions/browser/chromium/rules.mjs
    Interception decision pipeline: guarding against the extension's own,
    restored and stale downloads; the cancel-then-handoff sequence
    (downloads.cancel -> erase -> hand off to the host) with a single
    give-back-to-browser fallback only when the host is unreachable;
    per-download dedupe between the onDeterminingFilename and onCreated
    listeners; filename resolution and Content-Disposition parsing;
    HTML-response rejection; the signed-CDN release-host allowlist.
    Derived from:
      - src/linkgrabber/DownloadLinkInterceptor.ts
      - src/utils/ExtractFileNameFromHeader.ts
      - src/utils/ForbiddenHeaders.ts

  extensions/browser/chromium/background.js
    Listener wiring for downloads.onDeterminingFilename (primary) with
    downloads.onCreated as the Firefox fallback, the held/downloads-paused
    handoff ordering, and the alt-click bypass cache.
    Derived from:
      - src/background/background.ts
      - src/backend/nativemessaging/NativeMessagingTransport.ts
      - src/backend/NativeMessagingApi.ts

  extensions/browser/chromium/content.js
    Alt-click "send this link to the download manager" bypass.
    Derived from:
      - src/contentscripts/ContentScript.ts

  extensions/browser/chromium/rules.test.mjs
    Test cases covering the derived pipeline (GitHub release redirect chains,
    Google Drive confirm pages / drive.usercontent.google.com, and repeated
    downloads of the same URL).

  extensions/browser/firefox/rules.js
  extensions/browser/firefox/background.js
    Firefox ports of the two files above; the ES-module sources were adapted
    to classic scripts and the callback APIs to browser.* Promises.

The IDM-style download windows and the monotonic progress layer under
apps/desktop/ are original to SAYL and are not derived from AB Download
Manager. No code was taken from any GPL-licensed project (Gopeed, XDM, aria2,
Persepolis or others).

